  {
   "slug": "why-four-lasts",
   "title": "Why four lasts",
   "date": "2026-10-14",
   "categories": [
    "fit-notes"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "lasts"
   ],
   "image": "assets/images/demo/P07.webp",
   "excerpt": "A shoe fits only as well as the form it was shaped over, so we build across four.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A shoe can only fit as well as the form it was shaped over. Instead of stretching one standard shape across every runner, our partner factory builds across four lasts: Narrow, Standard, Wide and Open-toe.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Most feet land on Standard, and many people are surprised to find a different width in each foot. That is why every session tries three pairs on two lasts, two minutes each, before anything is chosen.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
  },
